From 3f07d32e249777965405c2606b834a41430fd8ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 06:43:46 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add a Wayland video layer under the window's surface

With MpvAbstractItem::videoLayer set, the video is drawn into a surface
of its own that is placed below the surface of the window, so that the
window can keep its controls, with alpha, over the video. Qt creates
subsurfaces only above their parent, so the layer is a wl_subsurface of
the window's wl_surface made here: synchronised, so that it is shown
with the window's next frame, taking no input, with an EGL surface of
its own on the OpenGL context of the scene graph. MpvRenderer draws into
it and swaps it before Qt swaps the window; the item itself stays
transparent.

The layer is only made on Wayland when the compositor has wl_subcompositor,
wp_viewporter and the stereo content declaration (the declaration comes
with a following change), everywhere else MpvQt works as before.
videoLayerSupported() tells before the first window exists whether it
will work, as the window needs an alpha buffer and a transparent color,
and videoLayerActive tells when it does.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet via Claude Code
